    <details class="table-view"><summary>Show as table</summary><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Wind (kn)</th><th>Chain (bow) (kgf)</th><th>Port line (kgf)</th><th>Stbd line (kgf)</th><th>Anchor load (kgf)</th><th>Side shift (m)</th><th>Chain lifted (m)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>10</td><td>160</td><td>4.8</td><td>149</td><td>146</td><td>1.55</td><td>33.8</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>250</td><td>0.0</td><td>256</td><td>236</td><td>2.35</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>378</td><td>0.0</td><td>403</td><td>364</td><td>2.83</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>25</td><td>555</td><td>37.8</td><td>563</td><td>540</td><td>3.15</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>764</td><td>103</td><td>733</td><td>750</td><td>3.42</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>997</td><td>187</td><td>914</td><td>982</td><td>3.68</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>1.2K</td><td>281</td><td>1.1K</td><td>1.2K</td><td>3.92</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>45</td><td>1.5K</td><td>379</td><td>1.3K</td><td>1.5K</td><td>4.14</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>50</td><td>1.8K</td><td>499</td><td>1.6K</td><td>1.8K</td><td>4.36</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>55</td><td>2.1K</td><td>622</td><td>1.8K</td><td>2.1K</td><td>4.56</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>60</td><td>2.5K</td><td>726</td><td>2.1K</td><td>2.4K</td><td>4.73</td><td>40.0</td></tr></tbody></table></details>"
`;

exports[`app renders the same output (golden master) > workedKgf > warnings 1`] = `
"
    <div class="alert alert-amber"><strong>Check the set-up</strong><ul><li>In the gust, all the chain is lifted off the seabed: the anchor is pulled upward and may break out.</li></ul></div>
    <div class="alert alert-info">
      <strong>⚠ These are static loads.</strong> A gust or a wave snatch load can be several times the static load. Turn on <strong>waves</strong> and, when swinging, <strong>fishtailing</strong> to see them.
      A sudden gust on an elastic mooring can overshoot to about <strong>1,788 kgf</strong> of wind load (2 × the gust increment).
      A 0.5 m/s surge stopped by the mooring adds about <strong>718 kgf</strong>.
      A nylon <strong>snubber</strong>, or longer nylon stern lines, adds elasticity and cuts snatch loads sharply. Try one in the Snubber section.
    </div>"
`;
